      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The effectiveness of a wealth tax in reducing inequality is debated; proponents argue it can significantly redistribute resources without directly impacting labor income, while opponents contend it may discourage high-net-worth individuals from investing and relocating their assets. Recent research suggests that these effects depend heavily on the tax's capital structure, including whether it is applied by bill or bill and if strong capital controls or global tax coordination exist to prevent capital flight. Ultimately, many policy experts recommend pairing a wealth tax with stimulus measures for the lower and middle classes to achieve meaningful inequality reduction without stalling economic growth.",
